"""Approximate the observed back/return family with local text rules.

Directional 'back' is negative, especially after 'fall'; a preceding article
or possessive weakens it. 'To' after back/return is strongly negative, whereas
'from' and 'side' after back are positive. Transparent compounds and written
back-like syllables receive separate estimates, including romanized syllables
in other scripts. Completing b + ide is positive. Unmatched tokens predict zero.
Only two preceding tokens are retained, and document boundaries reset them.
