At document starts, Latin continuations are usually negative, Cyrillic text
positive; brackets and module-opening keywords have separate baselines.
Away from starts the prediction is near zero, with small length/grammar
adjustments and an end-marker baseline. Extended arrowheads are strongly
negative; an opening HTML declaration is strongly positive. Word-specific
variation is intentionally omitted.
