"""Layer 1, MLP down-projection component 4724: the "o-i" spelling detector.

It fires when the letters o and i are spelled out, above all in a DOI reference.
Its activation goes negative on:
  - the DOI token itself ("doi", " doi", "DOI") in citations such as "... 12: 23-45. doi:10...",
    the strongest case (about -10);
  - the colon or ".org" straight after a doi token, as in "doi:10" or "doi.org" (about -5.5);
  - the library name "Joi" (about -7);
  - French words with "oi" or the pronoun "lui" as a whole word:
    moi, roi, loi, quoi, poi (about -2), lui (about -1.4);
  - a bare "oi" or capital "OI" piece (about -4), and "ois" / "oid" (about -1);
  - a bare "i" or "I" that completes an o-ending fragment across a token boundary:
    "PO|I", "Go|i", "Lo|i", "OIG-O|I" (about -5);
  - any other short i-initial fragment after an o-ending one: "Bo|is", "Charlevo|ix" (about -0.5).
At the first token of a document the activation is weakly positive (about +0.25).
Everything else is near zero.

The numbers are the average activation in each class, measured on training text. The
classes explain roughly a third of the variance on training text (about 0.29 on the eval
rows); the rest is small, context-dependent noise that these rules do not model.
A lookup table of every token's average activation would do somewhat better on held-out
text, but it is not a concept, so it is not used here.
"""

READS = ()

DOI_TOKENS = {"doi", "DOI"}
OI_WORDS = {"Joi": -7.4, "moi": -2.1, "roi": -2.1, "loi": -2.1, "quoi": -2.1, "poi": -2.1, "lui": -1.4}
OI_PIECES = {"oi": -4.0, "OI": -4.0, "Oi": -4.0, "ois": -1.0, "oid": -1.0}


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    tok = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    word = tok.strip()
    if len(prefix) == 1 or prefix.document_ids[-2] != prefix.document_ids[-1]:
        return carry, 0.25                      # first token of a document
    prev = prefix.token_strings[-2].strip()
    bare = not tok.startswith(" ")              # no leading space: inside a word
    after_o = prev[-1:] in ("o", "O")
    if word in DOI_TOKENS:
        return carry, -10.0
    if prev in DOI_TOKENS and word in (":", ".org"):
        return carry, -5.5
    if word in OI_WORDS:
        return carry, OI_WORDS[word]
    if bare and word in OI_PIECES:
        return carry, OI_PIECES[word]
    if bare and after_o and word[:1] in ("i", "I"):
        return carry, -5.0 if len(word) == 1 else -0.5
    return carry, 0.0

